## Data Flow Diagram

```
API ⟷ HabitsPage (Central State) ⟷ localStorage
  │
  ├─→ PastDayView (Read Only)
  │
  ├─→ TodayView (Database Sync)
  │    │
  │    └─→ User Interactions ──→ Database Update
  │
  └─→ FutureDayView (Local Storage)
       │
       └─→ User Interactions ──→ localStorage Update
```

## Implementation Tips

1. Start by implementing the basic structure without drag and drop
2. Add drag and drop once the basic layout works
3. Focus on Today view first, then expand to future and past
4. Test frequently with real data to catch issues early
5. Implement one piece at a time, ensuring each component works before moving on
6. Use console.log liberally during development to trace data flow

## Troubleshooting Common Issues

### React-DnD Issues
- Make sure `DndProvider` wraps all drag and drop components
- Only one backend can be active at a time
- Touch backend needs `{ enableMouseEvents: true }` for testing

### State Management Issues
- Use React DevTools to inspect component state
- Log state changes to understand the flow
- Verify API responses match expected formats

### CSS and Layout Issues
- Use browser dev tools to inspect element styling
- Test responsiveness with browser resize
- Verify CSS classes are applied correctly

